{"name":"Firecracker Salmon","hex":"#f36363","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"firecracker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small explosive device, typically containing a small amount of gunpowder in a tightly-wound roll of paper, primarily designed to produce a large bang.","A peanut butter cracker baked with marijuana, similar in concept to an Alice B. Toklas brownie."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firecracker"},{"term":"salmon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several species of fish, typically of the Salmoninae subfamily, brownish above with silvery sides and delicate pinkish-orange flesh; they ascend rivers to spawn.","A meal or dish made from this fish."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale pinkish-orange colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firecracker","blocks":[{"text":"A firecracker is a small explosive device primarily designed to produce a large amount of noise, especially in the form of a loud bang, usually for celebration or entertainment; any visual effect is incidental to this goal. They have fuses, and are wrapped in a heavy paper casing to contain the explosive compound. Firecrackers, along with fireworks, originated in China."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Firecrackers.png/330px-Firecrackers.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firecracker","wikidata":"Q588748"},{"title":"Salmon","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon are any of several commercially important species of ray-finned fish that can live in either freshwater or saltwater from the genera Salmo and Oncorhynchus of the family Salmonidae, native to tributaries of the North Atlantic (Salmo) and North Pacific (Oncorhynchus) basins. Salmon is a colloquial or common name used for fish in this group, but is not a scientific name. Other closely related fish in the same family include trout, char, grayling, whitefish, lenok and taimen, all coldwater fish of the subarctic and cooler temperate regions with some sporadic endorheic populations in Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Salmo_salar.jpg/330px-Salmo_salar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon","wikidata":"Q2796766"},{"title":"Salmon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon is a warm color ranging from light orange to pink, named after the color of salmon flesh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg/330px-SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2015138"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg/500px-Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg/1280px-Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg/500px-Beautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Large flower cracker set off at night","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeautiful_large_flower_cracker_creating_brilliant_light_and_sparkles_at_night.jpg"},{"